     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and most guidelines cap it at 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. An overdose carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for IR.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
